# Pinned external tools for check_external_checker.sh (sourced). The CI cache for the built tools
# is keyed on this file, so changing a revision rebuilds them.
# lean4export v4.34.0 writes export format 3.1.0; it is built with this repository's lean-toolchain.
LEAN4EXPORT_URL=https://github.com/leanprover/lean4export
LEAN4EXPORT_REV=076e8e57707e813375e8f9da8bf989799ace9680
# con-leche ae1f319 (2026-10-23; was c26f793 on 2026-10-22, dd695ca before): the revision behind the
# Lean Kernel Arena's published results (lean-kernel-arena@c534bac6: soundness 69 right, 0 wrong,
# 3 declined; completeness 131 right, 0 wrong, 6 declined). Built with its own lean-toolchain
# (v4.35.0, which carries the lean4#15288 thread-sharing fix); con-leche does not build with Lean
# 4.34.1 at any of these revisions. The gate runs it with --jobs=1.
# check_checker_pin_freshness.sh compares this pin and nanoda's with the Arena's.
CONLECHE_URL=https://github.com/leanprover/con-leche
CONLECHE_REV=ae1f31983ecd085c6140d0f8d433f23ee7eab72b
# nanoda 998e0a8 (2026-10-23; was e0d76f5): an independent Lean checker in Rust (no shared code with
# Lean or con-leche), at the revision behind the Arena's published results (lean-kernel-arena@c534bac6:
# soundness 72 right, 0 wrong, 0 declined; completeness 135 right, 0 wrong, 2 declined). Built with
# cargo; the thread stack is raised from 16 MiB to 256 MiB exactly as the arena patches it.
NANODA_URL=https://github.com/ammkrn/nanoda_lib
NANODA_REV=998e0a84e4c1572ca279ff05007af6ec6639405a
